# Project Governance (Mandatory)

Before implementing features or refactors, read:

1. `docs/00_Project_Governance/README.md`
2. `docs/00_Project_Governance/ENGINEERING_PLATFORM_V2.md` (until complete)
3. `docs/00_Project_Governance/PROJECT_ROADMAP.md`
4. `docs/00_Project_Governance/MODULE_OWNERSHIP.md`
5. `docs/00_Project_Governance/AI_DEVELOPMENT_GUIDELINES.md`
6. Domain docs under `docs/AI/Agents/<Domain>/` when relevant

Before coding, state: roadmap item → owning domain → allowed paths.

## Five layers

Product · Repository (Git) · Source ownership · Documentation · AI

## Standing rules

- Product Architecture ≠ Git Structure
- Source ownership mirrors Product Architecture
- New work: `feature/*` from roadmap via `develop`
- Investigations: `experiment/*` · Emergencies: `hotfix/*`
- Never modify unrelated modules or refactor without approval
- Never invent APIs or change backend contracts unless tasked
- Preserve Marketing ↔ Admin isolation
- Do not bypass `TESTING_CHECKLIST.md` for UI merges
- Do not start new product features until Engineering Platform v2.0 is complete
- While `ENGINEERING_FREEZE.md` is active: no features, no design polish, no refactors — release-blocking bugs only
- Do not use Foundation branches (`prototype-redesign`, `homepage-cursor-experiment`, `mobile-investigation`) for new work
- Do not rename/delete Foundation branches unless explicitly tasked
- Do not begin Repository Migration until stabilization report verdict is READY
